# Naam Dekho frontend environment.
#
# Copy to .env and fill in. Only variables prefixed VITE_ reach the browser,
# which also means anything you put here is PUBLIC. Never place a secret in
# this file. Server side keys belong in backend/.env.
#
#   cp .env.example .env

# Google Identity Services client id, used by the sign in button.
# Get it from Google Cloud Console, APIs and Services, Credentials, as an
# OAuth 2.0 Client ID of type "Web application". Add your dev origin
# (http://localhost:5173) and your production origin to Authorised JavaScript
# origins, or the button renders and then fails silently on click.
#
# The same value must be set as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID in backend/.env. The backend
# verifies the token server side against Google's JWKS, so a mismatch between
# the two shows up as a sign in that appears to work and then does nothing.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# The API origin is NOT configured here, and it is not read from the
# environment at all. Eight files each declare their own copy of
#
#   const API_ORIGIN = import.meta.env.DEV ? 'http://localhost:3000' : ''
#
# in src/admin/api.js, src/lib/useMe.js, src/lib/usePricing.js and the
# Account, Admin, Home, Pricing and SignIn pages. So the API is assumed to be
# on localhost:3000 in dev and same origin in production. Deploying the API to
# a different host means changing all eight, which is worth collapsing into one
# shared module first.
